From: jfacemyer <1776340+jfacemyer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 13:30:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 155/155] d2d1: Draw consecutive bitmaps with the same bitmap,
 interpolation and opacity together.

Affinity draws one bitmap per node of the path being edited, each with its
own transform: on a dense path, tens of thousands a frame, 91% with the
same bitmap as the one before. Each was a bitmap brush, a constant buffer
update, a vertex upload and a draw, and took 58% of the UI thread while
nodes were dragged.

Add such bitmaps to the draw batch instead: the vertices are transformed
on the CPU and carry their texture coordinates, so the constants are the
same for all of them, and one draw covers up to 16,384 bitmaps. Changing
the bitmap's content through CopyFromBitmap(), CopyFromMemory() or Map()
draws the batch first. WINE_D2D_NO_DRAW_BATCHING=1 turns it off with the
other batching.

DrawBitmap() in Affinity's node drag: 58% -> 10% of the UI thread, wined3d
37% -> 6%. d2d1 tests unchanged (17,521, 0 failures).
